---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  title="The Gambia: Plastic Loop"
  description="Plastic Loop Gambia establishes a locally rooted system for plastic collection, sorting, processing and manufacturing in the Greater Banjul Area, led by Hustle for Humanity Gambia."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal"><a href={base} style="color:inherit;">&larr; Plastic Circle West Africa</a></p>
      <h1 class="reveal">Plastic Loop, The Gambia</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        A locally rooted circular economy platform that turns plastic
        waste in the Greater Banjul Area into marketable products, local
        jobs and longer-term production capacity.
      </p>

      <div class="stat-bar">
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Plastic waste generated</p>
          <p class="stat-value">~23,000 t / year</p>
          <p class="stat-note">about 8.5 kg per person; plastic is ~9% of all municipal solid waste (UNDP, 2023)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Unmanaged plastic</p>
          <p class="stat-value">~75%</p>
          <p class="stat-note">leaks into the environment, rivers and the Atlantic Ocean (Common Seas, 2024)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Greater Banjul Area</p>
          <p class="stat-value">~1 million people</p>
          <p class="stat-note">the country's administrative, commercial and cultural hub</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Local context</p>
        <h2>Why The Gambia, why now</h2>
        <p>
          The Gambia is Africa's smallest mainland country, ranking 174th
          out of 193 on the Human Development Index, with a national
          poverty rate of around 48% (World Bank, 2022) and roughly 84% of
          employed youth in informal work (GBoS, 2023). Most waste goes to
          informal dumpsites or gets burned in backyards. Uncollected
          waste pollutes the River Gambia and its mangrove forests on its
          way to the Atlantic.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel wine" style="margin: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); width:auto; padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--blush);">Lead implementation partner</p>
    <h2>Hustle for Humanity Gambia</h2>
    <p style="max-width: 680px;">
      Hustle for Humanity Gambia (HFH-G), led by <strong>Musa Jallow</strong>,
      is the local implementation lead for Plastic Loop. The team handles
      day-to-day coordination, monitoring, community engagement and
      stakeholder mobilisation on the ground in the Greater Banjul Area.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">What makes Plastic Loop local</p>
        <h2>Built around The Gambia's own conditions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="pin" />
            <h3>A community collection network</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Clearly labelled plastic collection points sit at schools,
            markets and community centres, backed by regular collection
            drives run with schools, youth groups and women's
            associations.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="wave" />
            <h3>Energy built for the coast</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            The hybrid solar, battery and generator system is calibrated
            to the Gambian coast's seasonal solar profile, with separate
            dry-season and wet-season planning so that production
            continuity does not depend on grid power alone.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="users" />
            <h3>Designed with local businesses</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Product development happens together with local furniture
            makers, construction firms, hospitality operators and
            retailers, who help shape designs and also serve as
            distribution channels.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel wine" style="margin: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem); width:auto; padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); text-align:center;">
    <h2>Want to know more about Plastic Loop</h2>
    <p style="max-width:560px; margin: 0 auto 1.5em;">
      Get in touch to learn more about Plastic Loop, Hustle for Humanity
      Gambia, or the wider Plastic Circle West Africa programme.
    </p>
    <a class="pill-btn outline on-dark" href={`${base}contact`}>Get in Touch</a>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .pill-btn.outline.on-dark {
    border-color: var(--blush);
    color: var(--blush-pale);
  }

  .pill-btn.outline.on-dark:hover {
    background: var(--blush-pale);
    color: var(--wine-dark);
  }
</style>
